  "question": {
    "text": "If the chord $y=m x+1$ of the circle $x^2+y^2=1$ subtends an angle of measure $45^0$ at the major segment of the circle then value of $m$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "cbsFn",
      "text": "\n$2 \\pm \\sqrt{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Rz8hu",
      "text": "\n$-2 \\pm \\sqrt{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "UYt3v",
      "text": "\n$-1 \\pm \\sqrt{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ZHBde",
      "text": "\nnone of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Equation of circles $x^2+y^2=1=(1)^2$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow x^2+y^2=(y-m x)^2 \\Rightarrow x^2=m^2 x^2-2 m x y \\Rightarrow x^2\\left(1-m^2\\right)+2 m x y=0 \\\\\n& \\tan 45=\\pm \\frac{2 \\sqrt{m^2-0}}{1-m^2}=\\frac{\\pm 2 m}{1-m^2} \\Rightarrow 1-m^2=\\pm 2 m \\Rightarrow m^2 \\pm 2 m-1=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow m=\\frac{-2 \\pm \\sqrt{4+4}}{2}=\\frac{-2 \\pm 2 \\sqrt{2}}{2}=-1 \\pm \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
